      "releaseNotes": "Trip planning is smoother: place and stop selections return to the right field, search results stay above the keyboard, and destination markers respond more reliably. Includes refreshed Horários do Funchal timetables and route shapes from the September 7 update.",
      "version": "0.8.52",
      "wrapperType": "software",
      "currency": "GBP",
      "description": "Plan your Madeira bus trips before you arrive and check timetables when mobile signal is weak. Find routes, stops and scheduled departures for Funchal, airport journeys, levada walks and day trips.\n\nPlan from anywhere\n• Choose a place or bus stop as your origin and destination\n• Explore journeys without granting location access\n• See bus routes, walking connections and departure times before setting off\n\nTimetables that travel with you\n• Core schedules work offline after installation — tunnels, peaks, no signal\n• Browse weekday, Saturday, Sunday and public-holiday timetables\n• Next-bus countdown from the published timetable\n• Direction toggle for outbound and return\n• Times marked with ~ are estimates; departures are scheduled times, not live vehicle tracking\n\nExplore Madeira by bus\n• 60+ published routes across Horários do Funchal, CAM and RODOESTE\n• Airport connections and Aerobus (route 500) — €6.70 per person, cash on board\n• Monte via 020 / 021 (and 048 from Nazaré/Lido)• Fares screen for GIRO tickets and the separate Aerobus airport fare\n• Porto Santo ferry timetable and fares\n• Search by route number, stop, landmark, beach or hotel — EN / DE / FR / PT\n\nOn the bus\n• GO: tap \"I'm on this bus\" and follow your ride — next stop ahead, exit stop marked\n• Works offline. No account. No sign-up.\n\nCore planning and optional Pro\nCore timetables and trip planning work without an upgrade. Interactive route and journey maps and other Pro extras require an optional paid upgrade. The app shows available passes and prices before purchase.\n\nGood to know\nMadeira Bus is an independent planner, not the official SIGA app. It does not sell bus tickets. Madeira’s bus times and stops can change — always check the latest SIGA timetable and confirm departure and boarding place with local staff or the driver before relying on a journey, especially the last bus or a tight connection. If a stop, route or timetable looks wrong, send feedback from the app.\n\nSupport: support@madeirabus.com\nWeb: https://madeirabus.com\n• Trailheads and day trips — check trailhead bus options in the app (confirm boarding on the day)",
